<div class="article container container--narrow">
  <h1 class="page-title">The Unplug Challenge</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      These days, it seems like we fill every gap in our lives by scrolling away - in the subway, in the waiting room, during work breaks, in most of our free time... I could go on and on. It's hard to believe that just a couple of decades ago, people went about their days without the smartphones that are so ubiquitous today. We had entertainment, but television and desktop computers don't have nearly the convenience and pull of today's smartphones and social media platforms.
    </p>

    <p>
      As a result, we've become disconnected from the world around us. Time that would be spent with family is spent glued to screens. Instead of letting our minds rest, we overstimulate them at every turn. Social media keeps us up at night, stresses and worries us, and ruins our focus. The <b>Unplug Challenge</b> is a call to unplug from our screens and plug back into the real world.
    </p>

    <h2>Rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The challenge starts when you wake up in the morning, and ends on waking up the next day.</li>
      <li>No using screens of any kind, including (but not limited to) smart phones, tablets, TVs, and computers.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      It's as simple as that. The Unplug Challenge gives you a chance to engage with the world, to connect with friends, family, nature, the present moment, etc. It's also a no-risk way to get a glimpse of what your life would be like without screens. In the worst case scenario, you spend one day out of tens of thousands in your life to get an interesting, new experience - so why not?
    </p>

    <h2>Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Arrange plans beforehand with friends, in case you can't reach them without screens on the day of.</li>
      <li>Think of how you'd like to spend your time in advance, so you have activities to go for instead of sitting around not knowing what to do.</li>
      <li>Set a date as close as reasonable for the challenge - otherwise you might keep putting it off.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      So what are you waiting for? Get out there and live your life!
    </p>

  </div>
</div>
